{"availability":"available","full":"sinnercode228/flowdesk-crm","name":"flowdesk-crm","description":"Full-stack mini-CRM & sales dashboard: Next.js, Fastify, Prisma, PostgreSQL, JWT+RBAC, deals kanban, analytics. Live demo runs in the browser.","category":"Design","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-25T02:22:55Z","updated":"2026-10-15T14:09:52Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://sinnercode228.github.io/flowdesk-crm/","topics":["crm","fastify","jwt-auth","nextjs","postgresql","prisma","tailwindcss","typescript"],"demo":"https://sinnercode228.github.io/flowdesk-crm/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T23:48:55.701Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-15T23:48:55.701Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-15T23:48:55.701Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T07:01:43.919Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-15T23:48:55.701Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Next.js","Node.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A small CRM for a sales team: a deal kanban, contacts, a deal drawer with notes and history, a dashboard, and two roles, admin and manager. A Next.js static export talks to a Fastify and Prisma API, and a shared package between them holds the zod contract, the permission policy and the analytics functions.","I built this as a demo on generated data; it is not a client product. The name FlowDesk is made up, and every company, contact and deal comes from a seeded generator in packages/shared/src/demo-data.ts: e-mails on .example domains, phone numbers in the reserved 555-01XX range.","Demo: runs the same REST API inside the browser, with its state in localStorage, so there is no server behind it. The login form comes prefilled with the admin account, and the Manager button fills in the other one (admin@flowdesk.example and manager@flowdesk.example, password demo1234 for both). The Reset data button in the header restores the original data."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/sinnercode228/flowdesk-crm/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"16729afe67f5016bd771e6f37770b189be9fd569cb016b81d619af87e8b65394","extractedAt":"2026-10-15T23:48:55.805Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T23:48:55.805Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A small CRM for a sales team: a deal kanban, contacts, a deal drawer with notes and history, a dashboard, and two roles, admin and manager. A Next.js static export talks to a Fastify and Prisma API, and a shared package between them holds the zod contract, the permission policy and the analytics functions.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/sinnercode228/flowdesk-crm/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"The login form comes prefilled with the admin account, and the Manager button fills in the other one (admin@flowdesk.example and manager@flowdesk.example, password demo1234 for both).","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/sinnercode228/flowdesk-crm/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"POST /api/auth/refresh revokes the presented token and issues a new pair with the same familyId, which all tokens from one login share; replacedById links each row to its successor.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/sinnercode228/flowdesk-crm/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"api_key","status":"required","text":"The update only reports 0 rows after the winner's transaction has committed, so the refresh token the winner just got is revoked with the rest, and both callers log in again once their access token runs out.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/sinnercode228/flowdesk-crm/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"api_key","status":"required","text":"Cleanup on login deletes only families in which every token has expired, so a tab that keeps refreshing for weeks keeps every row of its chain, about one per access token lifetime while the user is active.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/sinnercode228/flowdesk-crm/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"16729af